{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Leiden communities (Traag, Waltman and van Eck 2019), maximizing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"quality"},{"type":"text","text":". Each level moves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices from a queue (shuffled by "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"generator"},{"type":"text","text":") to the community of greatest gain, refines"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each community from singletons by merging well-connected vertices at random (a merge of gain"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ΔH ≥ 0 drawn with probability proportional to exp(ΔH \/ "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"randomness"},{"type":"text","text":"), ΔH in units of edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight: m times the modularity gain, or the constant Potts model’s gain), and aggregates the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"refined communities into vertices. Iterations start from the last partition and repeat until"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one changes nothing (which leaves no vertex that gains by moving alone), or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"iterations"},{"type":"text","text":" of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"them have run. Every community is connected: refined communities grow only along edges, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"each community is finally split into its connected parts, which never lowers the quality."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Parallel edges add; a self-loop counts in degrees (modularity) or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inside its community, and never moves a vertex."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"leidenCommunities"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"quality"},{"kind":"text","text":": 